Section: Flying with a radio
  The T1-S VTOL flies with a radio. A RadioMaster TX15 (or another EdgeTX radio) in USB
  joystick mode gives the sim the sticks and the switches. The sim sends them to ArduPilot
  as the radio signals of a real receiver, so the plane reacts as it does with the real
  radio. [[ArduPilot]] reads the sticks and three switches: the arm switch, the mode switch,
  and the throttle stick. In the hover modes, the middle of the throttle stick holds the
  height. Above the middle the plane climbs, and below the middle it goes down.

  The first time, you do the calibration once (press F2 in the sim), and the sim saves it.
  After that, plug the radio in and start the station.

Background:
  Given the console is connected to a VTOL on the ground
  And the TX15 is ready
